From 1ce3205afb4b0462383f2b3eaa0d0c1e33cde492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 16:05:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07545/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5821: held-out
 live-path probe on sc25 (Generalization-Testing Floor class 1)

Ran the real scored E3AgentPolicy cascade cold against sc25 -- one of only
3 fully-solved public games with no registered GameAdapter -- to measure
how far the generic reusable live mechanism gets without any per-game
hand-tuning, versus the registry's hand-derived depth (6 levels).

Honest negative, not a harness gap: the mechanism genuinely stalled and
attempted induction once, but the induced dynamics model could not support
a usable plan (plan_found_rate=0.0, mean_heldout_accuracy=0.0), so
reached_level stayed 0. Independently corroborates, on a game outside the
prior 6-game roster, the standing project_arc_actions_to_progress_metric
finding that dynamics-induction quality is the binding constraint on the
frozen generator -- not per-game adapter absence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
